# Environment overrides for OpenList (QPKG).
#
# The service script sources this file (with `set -a`, so everything assigned
# here is exported to the daemon) before it starts OpenList. It is optional:
# with an empty file OpenList behaves normally.
#
# A syntax error in this file would break the start, so it is checked with
# `sh -n` first and the service refuses to start with a clear message.
#
# OpenList reads its configuration from the environment with the prefix
# OPENLIST_. Useful variables:
#
#   OPENLIST_ADMIN_PASSWORD   create the admin account on first start with this
#                              password instead of waiting for the web setup
#                              wizard. Only read when the account does not
#                              exist yet.
#   OPENLIST_HTTP_PORT         listen port. The service overrides this with
#                              QPKG_WEB_PORT (5244) — the QTS proxy has to
#                              agree with it.
#   OPENLIST_ADDR              bind address (0.0.0.0).
#   OPENLIST_SITE_URL          public URL of the instance.
#
# Example — set the admin password without the setup wizard:
#
#   OPENLIST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-please
#
